    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^2\\geq0>-4$, so $x^2>-4$ is true for all real $x$.",
      "worked": "The graph of $y=x^2$ lies entirely above the line $y=-4$. Therefore $x^2>-4$ holds for every real $x$, even though the equation $x^2=-4$ has no real solution.",
